# Canonical author identity for this repository.
#
# Git records the author name and email that were configured on the machine
# that made each commit, so a stray local config silently attributes work to a
# different account. This file pins every historical spelling to the account
# that owns the project; `git log`, `git shortlog -e` and GitHub all honour it,
# and git-filter-repo accepts it via --mailmap.
#
# To check:  git log --format="%an <%ae>" | sort -u
#             git shortlog -sne --all
#
# Keep the first line below last-resort: it renames anyone already using the
# canonical address.
